<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Sub-KG lifecycle: a knowledge graph staged as a directory inside a harnessed
  repository, declared as its own layer, that may later leave whole for a
  repository of its own.

  Source of truth: this file. The SVG beside it is generated from it by
  `bun run cat render:bpmn`; never hand-edit the SVG.

  The light sibling of kg-separation.bpmn. That process splits a graph into a
  content repository and a tools repository; this one moves a DATA layer
  whole. It keeps its own grow-in-place and staging steps and calls the phases
  the two share: kg-separation-authorise, kg-separation-move (whose seeding
  gateway is decisions/seed-readiness-gate.dmn) and kg-separation-cutover.

  TWO OWNER CONFIRMATIONS, BOTH NON-RELAXABLE. Creating the repository is
  visible outside this one and is not undone by a revert; deleting the in-repo
  copy removes a durable artefact. Each is preceded by a report of what would
  happen, how large it is and how it is undone (deletion-requires-confirmation),
  and each has a default that changes nothing.
-->
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:bootstrap.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/"
                  xmlns:cat-harness.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/processes/ns/"
                  id="Definitions_Process_SubKgLifecycle" targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows"
                  exporter="folio-assistant" exporterVersion="1">
  <bpmn:import namespace="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/" location="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns.jsonld" importType="http://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="administrator" name="Administrator (owner)"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="authoring-agent" name="Authoring agent"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="build-pipeline" name="Build pipeline"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="platform-authoring-agent" name="Platform authoring agent"/>
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_Process_SubKgLifecycle">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_Process_SubKgLifecycle" name="A sub-KG is staged in place, then leaves for its own repository" processRef="Process_SubKgLifecycle"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_SubKgLifecycle" name="A sub-KG is staged in place, then leaves for its own repository" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Create a knowledge graph inside a harnessed repository as a layer of its own, grow it there, and when it should leave, stage it for separation and move it whole into a new repository. Declared in place with a planned `repository` and a `livesAt` saying where it sits today; staged by one import seam (`&lt;name&gt;/platform.ts`), the separation guard and a self-contained rehearsal; then, each behind an explicit owner confirmation, the repository is created, the staged contents are copied in with their history, the declaration is re-pointed, a fresh clone is verified, and the in-repo copy is frozen in the kept trashcan.

The light sibling of kg-separation, which splits a graph into a content and a tools repository; this moves a data layer whole, and shares kg-separation's seeding gateway and decision table. DRAWN IN PHASES (owner, 2026-11-08, Q-B1-3 A): it keeps its own grow-in-place and staging steps, and calls the authorise, move and cut-over phases it shares with kg-separation.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <cat-harness.processes:policy enforcement="strict"/>
    </bpmn:extensionElements>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_Process_SubKgLifecycle">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Agent" name="Authoring agent" partitionElementRef="authoring-agent">
        <bpmn:documentation>Declares the sub-KG in place and grows it, reports what would move before each irreversible step, drains the open pull requests that keep the source from settling, and copies the staged contents into the new repository with their history.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_Wanted</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Brief</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Declare</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Grow</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Move</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Moved</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Platform" name="Platform authoring agent" partitionElementRef="platform-authoring-agent">
        <bpmn:documentation>The platform-side stages: pushing generic code and declarations down into the harness below, routing every climb out of the sub-KG through its one import seam, and re-pointing the declaration, the seam and the host's consumption once the new repository exists.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_PushDown</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Seam</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Pipeline" name="Build pipeline" partitionElementRef="build-pipeline">
        <bpmn:documentation>Runs the checks that decide the gateways: the separation guard and the three direction checks, the self-contained rehearsal, the seed-readiness table at seed time, and the gates of the new repository from a fresh clone. A check that could not run stops the process; it is never read as a pass.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Guard</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Rehearse</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Alone</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Unknown</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_PhaseUnknown</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Admin" name="Administrator (owner)" partitionElementRef="administrator">
        <bpmn:documentation>The person's decisions: whether the sub-KG leaves at all, whether the new repository may be created, and whether the in-repo copy may be deleted. An agent reports and waits at each, asks with numbered options and a default that changes nothing, and none of the three may be relaxed by a package.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_DecideLeave</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Leave</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Stays</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Authorise</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Authorised</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Declined</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ConfirmCutover</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Freeze</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Kept</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Cutover</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_CutOver</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Separated</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_Wanted" name="A sub-KG is wanted&#10;in this repository">
      <bpmn:documentation>A content type's creation skill asked whether the new graph goes in a new repository or inside this one, and the answer was inside this one. Or a graph already staged here is to be taken through the rest of its lifecycle.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F0</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_Brief" name="Brief the work" calledElement="GT_Brief">
      <bpmn:documentation>Here the work is a sub-KG: what it is, and why it is staged here rather than in a repository of its own.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F0</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Declare" name="Declare it in place,&#10;with its seam">
      <bpmn:documentation>`&lt;name&gt;/&lt;name&gt;.json` with name, version, `repository` (the planned home), `livesAt` (where it sits today), `needs`, and only the directories that exist, each declared with its files in one commit. `&lt;name&gt;/platform.ts` from the first commit, so no climb out of the directory ever needs rerouting. Scaffolded by `init-folio --staged &lt;path&gt;`, which writes those two files and nothing at the host root; never `--instance`, which writes a whole repository.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="sub-kg-lifecycle"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Grow" name="Grow it in place">
      <bpmn:documentation>The content type's own authoring process runs here, against the staged layer. Many sub-KGs never leave; this task can last as long as the graph does.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="sub-kg-lifecycle"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_DecideLeave" calledElement="Process_AskThePerson" name="Ask whether it&#10;should leave now">
      <bpmn:documentation>The owner decides, from what is measured, whether the sub-KG starts staging for separation now. Asked as numbered options with the recommended one first and a stated default: keeping it in place is the default, and is a real outcome.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="sub-kg-lifecycle"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F31</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Leave" name="Leave now?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads the owner's answer to the ask before it. Staying in place is the default and a real outcome.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F31</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F4</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Stays" name="Stays in place">
      <bpmn:documentation>The sub-KG stays staged in the host. Everything done so far is in place and reversible, and the process can be started again when it should leave.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F4</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_PushDown" name="Push generic&#10;down first">
      <bpmn:documentation>Move what is generic into the harness below before the seam is closed, and consolidate what the sub-KG needs into the harness it instantiates. Wrong-direction edges hide in declarations and data as well as imports: run check:import-direction, check:reference-direction and check:process-bindings.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="graph-detanglement"/>
        <cat-harness.processes:no-call reason="Uses the detanglement practice's direction checks on a layer already declared in place. graph-detanglement.bpmn starts from declaring a tangled sub-graph, which stage 1 of this process has already done."/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Seam" name="Route every climb&#10;through platform.ts">
      <bpmn:documentation>Every platform symbol the sub-KG uses is re-exported from `&lt;name&gt;/platform.ts`, so re-pointing the platform is a one-file edit. A merge from main is where new climbs arrive; reroute them here.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="sub-kg-lifecycle"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>F8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>F11</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Guard" name="Guard green,&#10;no edge up?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Decided by commands: instance-separation-imports.test.ts (every instance whose repository differs from its livesAt is covered), and the three direction checks adding nothing. Red goes back to the seam.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F8</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Rehearse" name="Rehearse&#10;self-contained">
      <bpmn:documentation>`bun run cat seed:ready --layer &lt;name&gt; --rehearse` copies the layer and what it needs into a scratch workspace of sibling directories and runs the tests there. Run the gates rather than scanning imports: a static scan misses files the gates load at run time, and renaming the directory changes every generated page.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="sub-kg-lifecycle"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F9</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Alone" name="Green alone?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Green with only the layer and what it needs present goes on. Red means a climb or a run-time load the guard did not see: back to the seam. If the rehearsal could not run, that is not a pass: stop.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F11</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F12</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F13</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Authorise" name="Authorise the&#10;move" calledElement="Process_KgSeparationAuthorise">
      <bpmn:documentation>Report what would move and how it undoes, and ask the owner to create the repository. Declining leaves it staged, ready to leave.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="deletion-requires-confirmation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F13</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F14</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Authorised" name="Authorised?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads which end the authorise phase reached.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F14</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F15</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F16</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Declined" name="Staged, ready&#10;to leave">
      <bpmn:documentation>Not yet. The sub-KG stays in the host, staged and rehearsed; nothing outside the repository changed.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F15</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Move" name="Move it into its&#10;repository" calledElement="Process_KgSeparationMove">
      <bpmn:documentation>Create the repository, drain, copy the staged contents in, re-point the declaration, verify a fresh clone, then consume, release and check every identifier dereferences.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="kg-separation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F16</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F17</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Moved" name="Moved and&#10;verified?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads which end the move phase reached. Nothing is seeded on an unknown readiness, and a fresh clone that could not run is not a pass.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F17</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F18</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F19</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_ConfirmCutover" calledElement="Process_AskThePerson" name="Ask to freeze the&#10;in-repo copy">
      <bpmn:documentation>The agent reports the files that would move, their size, the new repository and the commit the copy matches, then asks: (1) freeze it in the kept trashcan now, (2) keep in place until the first release, (3) show the file list first. Default if there is no answer: (2), nothing moves. A green fresh clone is the precondition for asking, not the answer. Non-relaxable. The host keeps a FROZEN copy in the kept trashcan, not a refreshed mirror and not a deletion; the live copy is the remote mount or subscription set up at stage 10.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <cat-harness.processes:policy relaxable="false"/>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="deletion-requires-confirmation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F18</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F27</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Freeze" name="Freeze it now?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads the owner's answer to the ask before it. Keeping in place until the first release is the default: nothing moves.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F27</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F28</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F29</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Kept" name="Consumed; in-repo&#10;copy kept">
      <bpmn:documentation>The host consumes the new repository and keeps its own copy, as the owner chose. The cutover can be asked again later.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F28</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Cutover" name="Cut over" calledElement="Process_KgSeparationCutover">
      <bpmn:documentation>Freeze the in-repo copy in the kept trashcan and measure the cutover until it is complete or cannot be shown complete.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="kg-separation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F29</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F30</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_CutOver" name="Cut over?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads which end the cutover phase reached: complete, or not shown complete.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F30</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F32</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F33</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Separated" name="Separated">
      <bpmn:documentation>The sub-KG lives in its own repository and the host consumes it from there.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F32</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Unknown" name="UNKNOWN: stop.&#10;Not clean">
      <bpmn:documentation>The rehearsal could not run. Reported as could-not-check, never as green.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F12</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_PhaseUnknown" name="UNKNOWN: stop.&#10;Not clean">
      <bpmn:documentation>A phase could not decide: seed readiness unknown, a fresh clone that could not run, or a cutover not shown complete. Reported as could-not-check, never as green.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F19</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>F33</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F0" sourceRef="Start_Wanted" targetRef="Task_Brief"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F1" sourceRef="Task_Brief" targetRef="Task_Declare"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F2" sourceRef="Task_Declare" targetRef="Task_Grow"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F3" sourceRef="Task_Grow" targetRef="Task_DecideLeave"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F31" sourceRef="Task_DecideLeave" targetRef="GW_Leave"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F4" name="stay" sourceRef="GW_Leave" targetRef="End_Stays"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F5" name="leave" sourceRef="GW_Leave" targetRef="Task_PushDown"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F6" sourceRef="Task_PushDown" targetRef="Task_Seam"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F7" sourceRef="Task_Seam" targetRef="GW_Guard"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F8" name="red" sourceRef="GW_Guard" targetRef="Task_Seam"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F9" name="green" sourceRef="GW_Guard" targetRef="Task_Rehearse"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F10" sourceRef="Task_Rehearse" targetRef="GW_Alone"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F11" name="red: an unseen climb" sourceRef="GW_Alone" targetRef="Task_Seam"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F12" name="could not run" sourceRef="GW_Alone" targetRef="End_Unknown"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F13" name="green" sourceRef="GW_Alone" targetRef="Call_Authorise"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F14" sourceRef="Call_Authorise" targetRef="GW_Authorised"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F15" name="declined" sourceRef="GW_Authorised" targetRef="End_Declined"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F16" name="authorised" sourceRef="GW_Authorised" targetRef="Call_Move"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F17" sourceRef="Call_Move" targetRef="GW_Moved"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F18" name="verified" sourceRef="GW_Moved" targetRef="Task_ConfirmCutover"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F19" name="unknown" sourceRef="GW_Moved" targetRef="End_PhaseUnknown"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F27" sourceRef="Task_ConfirmCutover" targetRef="GW_Freeze"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F28" name="keep" sourceRef="GW_Freeze" targetRef="End_Kept"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F29" name="freeze" sourceRef="GW_Freeze" targetRef="Call_Cutover"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F30" sourceRef="Call_Cutover" targetRef="GW_CutOver"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F32" name="complete" sourceRef="GW_CutOver" targetRef="End_Separated"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F33" name="could not determine" sourceRef="GW_CutOver" targetRef="End_PhaseUnknown"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_Process_SubKgLifecycle">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_Process_SubKgLifecycle" bpmnElement="Collaboration_Process_SubKgLifecycle">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Participant_Process_SubKgLifecycle" bpmnElement="Participant_Process_SubKgLifecycle" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="130" y="60" width="3780" height="1500"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Agent" bpmnElement="Lane_Agent" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="60" width="3750" height="250"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Platform" bpmnElement="Lane_Platform" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="310" width="3750" height="250"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Pipeline" bpmnElement="Lane_Pipeline" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="560" width="3750" height="500"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Admin" bpmnElement="Lane_Admin" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="1060" width="3750" height="500"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Start_Wanted" bpmnElement="Start_Wanted"><dc:Bounds x="272" y="167" width="36" height="36"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="240" y="209" width="100" height="40"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Brief" bpmnElement="Task_Brief"><dc:Bounds x="405" y="125" width="120" height="120"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Declare" bpmnElement="Task_Declare"><dc:Bounds x="580" y="125" width="120" height="120"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Grow" bpmnElement="Task_Grow"><dc:Bounds x="755" y="125" width="120" height="120"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
